    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. regarding the price adjustment mechanism, what should i look out for in terms of \"bad faith\" behavior from the supplier? like, how can i write the contract so they can't just use loopholes to jack up prices right when we need the materials most?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To guard against supplier bad faith, you need to make the price adjustment mechanism *highly* transparent and objective. Avoid vague language; the contract should specify *exactly* which indices or cost components trigger an adjustment and under what conditions. You can include a \"Good Faith Negotiation Period\" requirement before any unilateral price hike takes effect. This forces them to actually discuss the change rather than just slamming a new invoice on your desk.",
      "source": "target",
